ession_utils.py` — shared session path logic and state I/O\n- Extract `host/constants.py` — all magic numbers as named constants\n- Fix import ordering in `host/cli.py` (move `core.review` import to top, `shutil` to top)\n- Add missing `start()`/`stop()` to `Notifier` Protocol\n- Remove unused `AgentEventType` values or implement them\n- Write tests for `host/cli.py` cmd_accept/cmd_reject (biggest coverage gap)\n\n### Phase 2 — Split the watcher\n- `host/watcher.py` `HostWatcher` → split into:\n  - `ContainerManager` — Docker pause/unpause\n  - `QACoordinator` — answer collection, waiting signals\n  - `ReviewOrchestrator` — auto-review launch, verdict extraction\n  - `SessionCleaner` — orphan detection, cleanup\n  - `AutoStartWatcher` — issue polling, launch gating\n- Each class gets its own test file\n\n### Phase 3 — Refactor launch and CLI\n- `host/launch.py` `main()` → extract `WorkspaceSetup`, `IssueDataDumper`, `DockerOrchestrator`\n- `host/cli.py` `cmd_accept()` → extract `MergeExecutor`, `ConflictValidator`\n- Wrap `subprocess.run()` calls in `host/git_utils.py` and `host/docker_utils.py`\n\n### Phase 4 — Split config\n- `core/config.py` → `core/config/models.py` (dataclasses), `core/config/loader.py` (YAML parsing), `core/config/factories.py` (adapter instantiation)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] All phases complete\n- [ ] Coverage \u003e= 80% (`coverage run -m pytest tests/ \u0026\u0026 coverage report`)\n- [ ] No function \u003e 50 lines\n- [ ] No class with 5+ unrelated responsibilities\n- [ ] No magic numbers — all timeouts/thresholds are named constants\n- [ ] All imports at module top (except documented circular-dep breaks)\n- [ ] All tests pass","files":null}]}